\theta+3\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi}{2}<\\theta\\le 3\\pi\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ in the comparison blanks.\n\nThe range of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is:\n\n{{field-5}} {{field-6}} $y$ {{field-7}} {{field-8}}." 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747312 1072 #uuid "06418a1e-a69a-5340-82ce-0ac7735c356c" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747312 1074 "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=-1$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=3\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included).\n\nThe value $-1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$.\n\nMultiply by $4$ and translate by $-2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &<\\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n-4 &<4\\sin\\theta\\le 4 \\\\\n-6 &<4\\sin\\theta-2\\le 2 \\\\\n-6 &<x\\le 2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-6<x\\le 2$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=3\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=-1$ (included).\n\nThe value $-1$ is attained at $\\theta=3\\pi$.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=2\\pi$.\n\nMultiplying by $-5$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $3$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n5 &\\ge-5\\cos\\theta\\ge-5 \\\\\n8 &\\ge-5\\cos\\theta+3\\ge-2 \\\\\n-2 &\\le y\\le 8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-2\\le y\\le 8$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value." 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747313 1080 "-3" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747313 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747313 1083 #uuid "06f99399-7c0b-5b90-8f6e-7afa79522040" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186747464 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747314 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747314 1077 "field-3" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747314 1078 #edb/ref 17592186747464 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747314 1079 #uuid "075c5c18-de0c-52fb-bd58-d3c4c41baa12" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747315 1080 "0" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747315 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747315 1083 #uuid "0778145e-0b36-5aba-b9e6-215cd309f577" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747316 1080 "<" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747316 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747316 1083 #uuid "083dbd93-c4f7-5e8c-874f-d9cea0bed686" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747320 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747404 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747407 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747441 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747473 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747486 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747506 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747510 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sin\\theta-1\n$$\n\n$$\ny=-4\\cos\\theta-1\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi}{2}<\\theta<\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ in the comparison blanks.\n\nThe range of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is:\n\n{{field-5}} {{field-6}} $y$ {{field-7}} {{field-8}}." 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1072 #uuid "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747317 1074 "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=-1$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=1$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $-1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nMultiply by $2$ and translate by $-1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &<\\sin\\theta<1 \\\\\n-2 &<2\\sin\\theta<2 \\\\\n-3 &<2\\sin\\theta-1<1 \\\\\n-3 &<x<1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-3<x<1$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $0$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=2\\pi$.\n\nMultiplying by $-4$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-1$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0 &<\\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n0 &>-4\\cos\\theta\\ge-4 \\\\\n-1 &>-4\\cos\\theta-1\\ge-5 \\\\\n-5 &\\le y<-1.\n\\end{aligned}