{5}{2}$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-2$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n\\frac{5}{2} &\\ge-\\frac{5}{2}\\sin\\theta\\ge-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{2} &\\ge-\\frac{5}{2}\\sin\\theta-2\\ge-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\\n-\\frac{9}{2} &\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-\\frac{9}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\cos\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiplying by $-3$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $2$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n3 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta\\ge-3 \\\\\n5 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta+2\\ge-1 \\\\\n-1 &\\le y\\le 5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-1\\le y\\le 5$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value." 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747309 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747360 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747442 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747445 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747469 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747471 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747481 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1068 #edb/ref 17592186747488 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139545113 17592186576411 true] [17592186747403 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-4\\cos\\theta+2\n$$\n\n$$\ny=-2\\sin\\theta-3\n$$\n\n$$\n0<\\theta<\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ in the comparison blanks.\n\nThe range of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-